' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeControlEventService.java :: accept.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeExecutionControlRepository.java :: markConfirming, acceptConfirmation, claimConfirmation.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeSessionControlDispatcher.java :: dispatchConfirmation.
' Observed behavior: tool confirmation closes one response and resumes through a new fixed segment.
' Design reason: plan review reuses this transport and durable handoff.
' Java divergence: immutable plan event identity is the approval target; tool permissions remain separate.
title CampusClaw Plan Review - Target Sequence
actor User
participant "Runtime client" as UI
participant "POST Events\naccepting instance" as API
participant "Plan review service\nand persistence" as Service
database GaussDB as DB
participant "Control dispatcher\noriginal instance" as Dispatcher
participant "Original execution\nExitPlanMode / Agent" as Agent

group 1. Publish a plan in the active root
  Agent --> UI : Stream ordinary assistant Markdown (pending change)
  Agent -> Agent : Same response: one ExitPlanMode({}) call after text
  Agent -> Service : Commit message, then call; bind immutable source snapshot
  Agent -> Service : beginReview(proposalSnapshotDTO)
  Service -> DB : Lock Session and execution; validate active plan mode
  Service -> DB : Append agent.plan + confirming idle;
  note right of DB
  Same transaction records the internal pending
  plan
  and closes the current segment.
  Session remains running.
  end note
  DB --> Service : Commit
  Service --> UI : Original SSE: plan, confirming idle; close
  Agent -> Agent : Await plan decision; keep tools and current prompt
end

== 2. Accept one review decision ==
User -> UI : Approve or revise
UI -> API : POST user.plan_confirmation(targetEventId, result)
API -> API : Reserve response / result wait capacity
API -> Service : Accept decision
Service -> DB : Lock Session and execution;
note right of DB
  Require the exact pending plan in this Session.
  Recheck root, branch, current segment and stop
  state.
end note
Service -> DB : Append confirmation; create continuation segment;
note right of DB
  Approve: update mode=build and append mode
  event.
  Revise: keep mode=plan and persist feedback.
  Clear pending plan. Keep Session running.
end note
DB --> Service : Commit fixed continuation target
Service --> API : Accepted confirmation
API --> UI : First SSE frame: full committed confirmation
API -> Dispatcher : Local notify if original execution is local
note over DB,Dispatcher
  Existing database control polling is the
  fallback.
  The accepting instance does not reconstruct
  credentials.
end note
== 3. Resume the original execution ==
Dispatcher -> DB : Claim decision for fixed target
DB --> Dispatcher : Committed decision, once
Dispatcher -> Agent : Bind new segment output; complete pending Future
alt Approved
  Agent -> Agent : Recompose captured BASE + Main Agent role + BUILD
  Agent -> Service : Persist ExitPlanMode result approved=true
  Agent -> Agent : Next step: TODOs and implementation
else Revision requested
  Agent -> Service : Persist normal result approved=false and feedback
  Agent -> Agent : Continue plan; use new plan eventId
end
Service --> UI : New SSE: committed mode/result/output via local or DB path
note over UI,Agent
  Every agent event keeps the original message
  sourceEventId.
  A new confirming or actual terminal idle closes
  this response.
  Disconnect closes observation only; it never
  grants approval.
end note
@enduml

